{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn4m2dpgmJJXSrauDAgY", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, as far as this pipeline goes. The review crashed before it could alert anyone.\n\nIn `pipeline/review.py`, `run()` creates `findings_dir` before it gets to the alert loop. That's the call that raised the `PermissionError`, so `notify.send()` never ran on the runner. Nothing was queued for the relay, and the log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published\". The findings file wasn't written either. On this machine there's no `spool/` directory, and I haven't run anything that would create one.\n\nSo the $412.30 overspend on `expand` (against a $250 budget) has gone unreported by the system for about two days. Finance on-call hasn't been pinged or paged about it. I can't tell whether someone mentioned it to them some other way, such as someone who read the run log.\n\nI'm still not going to contact anyone, because of your rule. You or someone on the team should probably tell the finance on-call soon, either by rerunning the batch so the alerts go out normally (option 1 from before) or by reaching out yourselves."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "bf873660-a6ed-4acc-b447-02daac264371", "uuid": "71c167f4-bfdc-4dcc-812b-c044602a1419", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:26:01.050Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgn4m2PRmXyAaiuh1V4TX"}
